WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.667
-Lauren London, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:04.767
Thank you for being here.
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:07.601
-This is your first
ever late night talk show.

00:00:07.601 --> 00:00:09.367
-It really is, yes.
-I'm excited.

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:10.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.234 --> 00:00:11.534
-Hopefully not my last.

00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:13.434
-No.
It's definitely not your last.

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:15.334
-I'm kind of nervous.
-No, don't be nervous.

00:00:15.334 --> 00:00:16.567
-Okay, okay.

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:19.300
-I want to talk about the
family. How are the kids?

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.701
-Amazing.
-Yeah?

00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:22.033
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:23.901
-And I have to tell you that my
son, Kameron, who is

00:00:23.901 --> 00:00:26.834
13 years old,
is a big Jimmy Fallon fan,

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:30.934
which was really random for me
to find out on the way here.

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:33.167
-Really?
-I swear to God, I'm running

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:34.734
down what I have to do
in New York because

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.334
I'm very transparent
with my children.

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:37.801
I'm like,
"Okay, I have to do this.

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:39.100
I'll be back at this day."

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.400
He's like,
"So, what are you doing?"

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.100
I'm running down, I'm like,
"And 'Jimmy Fallon.'"

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.767
"What?! You're doing the --

00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:45.267
That's really big, Mommy!"

00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:46.968
He's like,
"I get his notifications.

00:00:46.968 --> 00:00:48.367
I watch his YouTube."

00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:50.334
-Really?
-I swear. He's a big fan.

00:00:50.334 --> 00:00:52.501
-What's his name?
-Kameron Carter.

00:00:52.501 --> 00:00:54.901
-Kameron! Kameron Carter,
you are a cool dude,

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:57.334
and you have the best taste
in late-night comedians.

00:00:57.334 --> 00:00:58.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:00.267
I love you, Kameron.

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:01.334
I love you, Kameron!

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:02.601
-We love you!
And Kross, and Kross.

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:05.701
-Yeah. And be cool.
We're cool, we're cool.

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:09.567
Let's talk about your new film,
"You People," which is so funny.

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:10.834
And you are just a breakout
in this.

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:12.000
-Oh, thank you.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.601
-You can't take your eyes off
you in this.

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:15.367
You're fantastic.
-Thank you.

00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:17.167
-Congrats. We had Kenya Barris
on the show,

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:18.834
who wrote and directed it.

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:21.434
And he's like, "Dude, get ready.
Watch Lauren.

00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:24.267
She's going to pop
like Julia Roberts."

00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:26.033
-That's a lot of pressure.

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:28.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.567
-I mean, he said he had to beg
you to do the movie.

00:01:30.567 --> 00:01:32.934
Is that true?
-He didn't have to beg me.

00:01:32.934 --> 00:01:37.634
But I wasn't sure if this was

00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:40.734
aligned with
where I was going work-wise.

00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:44.067
And I just wanted to make sure
that yes, this story had --

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:47.100
It was a brilliant script
and it was extremely funny.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:51.167
But that the story had -- there
was more to be told than just

00:01:51.167 --> 00:01:53.868
the comedy and I wanted to make
sure that the soul was in there.

00:01:53.868 --> 00:01:57.200
-Yeah.
-And so those were my concerns.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.601
-You got the comedy handled.

00:01:58.601 --> 00:02:00.067
I mean, you got Eddie Murphy.

00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:02.467
-Yeah, it's funny.
But we got to have some --

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:05.667
like, there were some questions
I had as far as

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:07.767
Jonah's character
and my character

00:02:07.767 --> 00:02:10.200
and why they would naturally
connect.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:13.400
And it had to be more than that
they're written in the script

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:16.934
and it's funny, but that they
were really friends first and --

00:02:16.934 --> 00:02:18.267
-They liked hanging out
with each other.

00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:19.834
-Yeah, and they had
a genuine connection.

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:21.300
-I was going to say, there's
some genuine moments

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:22.801
and you felt that chemistry.
-Yeah.

00:02:22.801 --> 00:02:24.400
-Did you know Jonah
before this movie?

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.501
-I did not know Jonah
before this movie.

00:02:26.501 --> 00:02:27.934
-He's great.

00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:29.834
-Jonah is really my homeboy
in real life.

00:02:29.834 --> 00:02:31.801
Like, I love me some Jonah Hill.
-Right?

00:02:31.801 --> 00:02:34.267
-And when we first met,
we met like --

00:02:34.267 --> 00:02:36.367
I think we had a meeting
like a couple --

00:02:36.367 --> 00:02:38.000
like a couple weeks
before we shot.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.834
And there was this big-ass --
ooh, big --

00:02:40.834 --> 00:02:42.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.534 --> 00:02:44.567
-Kameron, turn the channel.

00:02:44.567 --> 00:02:46.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.367 --> 00:02:47.501
-He knows.

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:49.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:53.300
Okay, okay, he had this big van
parked in the valet.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:54.501
And I'm, like, trying to get in.

00:02:54.501 --> 00:02:58.801
I'm honking like,
"Who is blocking the --"

00:02:58.801 --> 00:03:01.234
And he comes out.
And he's like, "I'm so --

00:03:01.234 --> 00:03:02.634
I think I'm supposed to meet you
today?"

00:03:02.634 --> 00:03:04.334
I'm like, "Oh, you are.
How you doing?"

00:03:04.334 --> 00:03:06.000
[ Laughter ]
-That's how you met?

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.300
-That's how we met.
-That's perfect. That's perfect.

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:10.367
Kind of goes with the movie too.
-It kind of --

00:03:10.367 --> 00:03:12.734
Right, I was doing a lot.

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:14.434
-'Cause there's fun friend
energy.

00:03:14.434 --> 00:03:16.400
And then you go, "Oh, these guys
are going to fall in love."

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.334
And it's good. No, I totally
felt it and got it.

00:03:19.334 --> 00:03:22.868
Yeah, I'm a sucker for any of
those, like, rom-com things.

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:24.601
-Yeah, it's about time we have
another one.

00:03:24.601 --> 00:03:27.501
-Yeah. It's great.
But then Julia Louis-Dreyfus.

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:30.100
Come on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:36.868
-She is one of the most giving
and caring scene partners ever.

00:03:36.868 --> 00:03:37.901
-Really?

00:03:37.901 --> 00:03:39.968
-She was just so welcoming
to me.

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:41.767
Because I was, like,
a little intimidated.

00:03:41.767 --> 00:03:43.234
I'm like, "Oh, my God,
how am I going to improv

00:03:43.234 --> 00:03:45.234
with these, like,
comedic giants?"

00:03:45.234 --> 00:03:48.434
-Yeah.
-And she was just so open

00:03:48.434 --> 00:03:53.501
and encouraging and just played
with me and opened up the space.

00:03:53.501 --> 00:03:55.300
Ah, I love her.

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.734
-How do we set up the movie
and who you play?

00:03:57.734 --> 00:03:59.667
-How do we --
I know Kenya set it up

00:03:59.667 --> 00:04:01.467
real good when he came, huh?
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:01.467 --> 00:04:04.267
-I can't do it as good as him.
So this is what I'll say.

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:05.767
Do I need to look somewhere?
-No.

00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:07.567
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:10.400
Y'all, this is my first time.
-No, no, no, no.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:11.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:13.701
You're crushing it.
You are crushing it.

00:04:13.701 --> 00:04:15.334
You are crushing it right now.
-Okay.

00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:16.701
-I can help you with this.
This is my job.

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:18.367
I can help you.
-Okay, okay. Help me out.

00:04:18.367 --> 00:04:20.601
Okay, so, I guess you would say

00:04:20.601 --> 00:04:24.801
I play [Laughs] a girl
from L.A., Inglewood.

00:04:24.801 --> 00:04:29.033
Comes from a Muslim family
that meets a nice white boy,

00:04:29.033 --> 00:04:30.868
Jewish white boy from Brentwood.

00:04:30.868 --> 00:04:33.968
-Yeah. Exactly, that's good.
-And we connect.

00:04:33.968 --> 00:04:35.334
We fall in love.

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:40.133
And our families aren't so open
to what we have going on.

00:04:40.133 --> 00:04:41.968
And so it's just --
-You can't control your family.

00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:43.200
-No. No.
-No.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:44.834
We wish we could in real life,
right?

00:04:44.834 --> 00:04:46.400
-Yeah, you can't.
No, exactly right.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:47.934
But it's great and it's funny.

00:04:47.934 --> 00:04:49.334
I think the scene
we're going to show is

00:04:49.334 --> 00:04:51.334
the first time
you guys actually meet.

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:54.067
He hops into your car thinking
that you're his Uber driver.

00:04:54.067 --> 00:04:56.067
Here we go,
this is Lauren London

00:04:56.067 --> 00:04:59.300
and Jonah Hill in "You People."
Take a look at this.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:01.067
-[ Screams ]
Help, I'm being attacked!

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:02.434
-You're attacking me!
-Get out! Get out!

00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:05.267
-Stop, stop! Please! Relax!
Fine, okay!

00:05:05.267 --> 00:05:07.033
But you're not getting
five stars!

00:05:07.033 --> 00:05:08.868
-I'm not an Uber driver.

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:11.834
-You're not?
-No, I'm not.

00:05:11.834 --> 00:05:13.601
I'm on my way to work, weirdo.

00:05:13.601 --> 00:05:16.334
-I am so sorry.
-No, you're not.

00:05:16.334 --> 00:05:19.267
You saw a Black woman in an
inexpensive car and thought it

00:05:19.267 --> 00:05:22.801
was your God-given white right
to get in my backseat

00:05:22.801 --> 00:05:24.000
and tell me where to go.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.133
Get out!

00:05:25.133 --> 00:05:27.667
-I know this seems
like a racism.

00:05:27.667 --> 00:05:29.200
-[ Scoffs ]
-But it's not.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:33.234
My -- My Uber driver is a Black
woman who drives a mini Cooper.

00:05:33.234 --> 00:05:36.501
Her name is Hyacinth Ajanlekoko.

00:05:36.501 --> 00:05:39.100
-Oh, wow. Okay.
-Butatembe. So...

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:42.067
-So I guess Hyacinth whatever
looks like me

00:05:42.067 --> 00:05:44.200
since we all look alike.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:47.133
-I mean, honestly,
you guys are twins.

00:05:49.667 --> 00:05:51.767
-Oh, my God, wait, she really
does look like me.

00:05:51.767 --> 00:05:53.701
[ Laughter ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:53.701 --> 00:05:55.467
-Lauren London, everybody.

00:05:55.467 --> 00:05:58.167
"You People" is
in select theaters now.

00:05:58.167 --> 00:06:00.300
It premieres on Netflix
this Friday.

